<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59010" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόπρος</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>excrement, ordure</i>, of men and
			cattle, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.329
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.22
			</span></i>, etc.: in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Euph.
				96.4
			</span></i>; esp. as used in husbandry, <i>dung, manure</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				334a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				2.7.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>filth, dirt</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυλινδόμενος κατὰ κόπρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.414
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				24.640
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1116.14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B. C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>dunghill, byre</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.575
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.411
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				178
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθίσαι τινὰς ἐπὶ κόπρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					544.5
				</span></i>
			. (In this sense oxyt. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοπρός</span>
			acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1165.15
			</span></i>.) (Cf. Skt. <i>śákṛt</i>,
			gen. <i>śaknás</i> 'excrement'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
